# Contact form delivery goes through Atlas (Empreus's platform), not Resend.
# Mint the per-client key in Atlas under:
#   Clients > client > Documentation > API > Atlas
# The key is scoped to one sending domain and a fixed recipient allowlist.
# Never prefix it with NEXT_PUBLIC_ — that ships it to every visitor.
# Without a key the form still accepts submissions but emails nothing
# (logged to the console in dev).
ATLAS_API_KEY=

# Must be an address Atlas authorises for this key, as a BARE address —
# Atlas compares it exactly, so "Name <addr>" is rejected with a 403.
# Allowed for this key: DoNotReply@ or web@capitalhoardings.com.au
# Defaults to DoNotReply@capitalhoardings.com.au.
# CONTACT_FROM=DoNotReply@capitalhoardings.com.au

# Where enquiries go. Must be on the key's allowlist in Atlas or it 403s.
# Comma-separate for several. Defaults to office@capitalhoardings.com.au.
# CONTACT_TO=office@capitalhoardings.com.au

# Override only if Atlas moves. Defaults to https://atlascontrol.io/api/email/send
# ATLAS_ENDPOINT=

# Cloudflare Turnstile (optional). The API only enforces the check once
# TURNSTILE_SECRET_KEY is set, so the form keeps working until you configure it.
# Server-side verification only for now — adding the widget to the form would
# also need NEXT_PUBLIC_TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY and a change to ContactForm.tsx.
# TURNSTILE_SECRET_KEY=
